     "tipo": "texto",
     "titulo": "Ch. 21–30. A hike in the rain",
     "frases": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "週末、友達 と 山 へ 行く 予定 でした が、朝 から 雨 が 降って いました。友達 は「雨 でも 行ける んじゃないか」と 言いました。山 の 道 は ぬれていて 危ない ので、私たち は 駅 の 近く の 博物館 に 行きました。帰り に、友達 は「予定 を 変えた おかげで、新しい 展示 を 見られた」と 喜びました。",
       "alumno": "On the weekend I was planning to go to the mountains with a friend, but it had been raining since the morning. My friend said: \"Couldn't we go even if it's raining?\" As the mountain path was wet and dangerous, we went to a museum near the station. On the way back, my friend was delighted and said: \"Thanks to changing the plan, we were able to see a new exhibition.\"",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
